<title>MACAU: Macau and the Philippines initial air accord.</title>
<headline>Macau and the Philippines initial air accord.</headline>
<dateline>MACAU 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Macau and the Philippines have initialled an open-ended air services agreement allowing Air Macau and a Philippines airline to operate routes between both places, the Macau Civil Aviation Authority said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Philippines government, however, still has to designate which airline would be given the right to fly to Macau.</p>
<p>Portuguese-run Macau reverts to Chinese rule in December 1999. The agreement would be submitted to a Sino-Portuguese body handling handover details for approval before it can be formally signed.</p>
<p>--Hong Kong newsroom (852) 28436441</p>
